course: dictionary
lesson: 9717
title: Summary: the short version
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A summary is a short version of something longer. It gives only the main points, so you learn what happened without every detail. «A summary tells the main events in a few words, not every detail.» Think of it as the bones of a story, without all the extra flesh.
explain: A summary leaves things out on purpose. «A summary leaves things out, and a bot's summary can even get the story wrong.» A summary is useful, but it is not the whole book. If you need the full picture, go back to the original.
explain: You can also say «in summary», which means «to put it briefly». In school you may be asked to write a summary of a story or a chapter. Ask yourself: is it short, and does it give only the main points?
fact: A summary is a short version of something longer, giving only the main points.
fact: «In summary» means «to put it briefly».
fact: «A summary of a news report sticks to the facts and leaves out your own opinions.»
fact: Summary can also be an adjective in a formal way: «summary justice» means justice done quickly, without the usual steps.
fact: The plural of summary is summaries.
exercise: «A summary tells the main events in a few words, not every detail.» What is a summary? | A long story with lots of extra characters | Every single detail, word for word | *A short version that gives only the main points | A picture drawn on the cover
exercise: «A summary of a news report sticks to the facts and leaves out your own opinions.» What should a summary of a news report leave out? | The facts | The main events | *Your own opinions | The key points
exercise: What does «in summary» mean? | *To put it briefly | To write it very slowly | To make it longer | To read it out loud
test: «A summary leaves things out, and a bot's summary can even get the story wrong.» Why should you check the original book if you need the full picture? | Because the book is shorter | Because summaries are always perfect | Because summaries are always longer than the book | *Because a summary leaves things out
test: What is the plural of summary? | *summaries | summarys | summariess | summaryes
exam: In «summary justice», what does summary mean? | A very old, famous court case | *Done quickly, without the usual steps | A short written version of a story | A list of totals in a table
